msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:188
msgid "A positive X moves the icon right and a positive Y moves it down; negative values move it left and up. Both fields work the same way on either side."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:193
msgid "Per position"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:194
msgid "An offset belongs to the position, so all three stages that use that position share it. Reset returns it to the placement the position’s name promises."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:199
msgid "Facing the other way"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:200
msgid "Some icons — an arrow, a hand, a face — point one way. Every stage has a Flip horizontally checkbox that mirrors that stage’s icon, in the editor and on your site, without changing the library asset or any other stage."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:208
msgid "Editor and your site"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:209
msgid "Why the same icon can look slightly different in the two places."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:214
msgid "Measured, not assumed"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:215
msgid "The icon is placed by measuring the title’s real text on the page it is drawn on, so your theme’s font, weight and size decide the gap. A theme cannot move the icon wrongly, because nothing about it is guessed in advance."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:221
msgid "The preview may look different"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:226
msgid "The block editor draws the title in your theme’s own type only when the theme shares its styles with the editor. When it does not, the canvas uses the editor’s font and size instead. The icon keeps its place on the letters as the title changes size, so a nudge means the same thing in both — but the letters themselves are drawn differently, and no setting can change that: the published page shows your theme’s type."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:232
msgid "When there is no room beside the title"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:237
msgid "The icon stands beside the title in the space your theme leaves around the heading. A card in a widget owns that space instead, and may cut off whatever leaves it. Settings → Fit icons inside tight cards decides whether a card draws an icon smaller so it fits, or leaves it exactly as you placed it."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:243
msgid "In front of your theme’s layers"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:248
msgid "The icon is drawn above the title’s words already. If your theme stacks its own elements over the heading — a ribbon, a badge, a hover overlay — Settings → Icon stacking order decides where the icon belongs among them. 0 is the page’s normal order, a higher number brings it forward and a negative one sends it behind; the editor and your site use the same number."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:254
msgid "Offsets grow with the title"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:256
msgid "An offset is a distance on the title, so it is measured against the title’s font size — like the gap, and like the letters the icon sits over. A nudge you settle on in the editor is the same part of the same letter on the page, whichever size your theme draws the title at there."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:261
msgid "Titles that wrap"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:262
msgid "A title that wraps onto a second or third line is measured again, so the icon keeps the place you gave it. By default it is anchored to the first line: your X and Y count from that line, a side icon sits beside that line’s own words rather than beyond the longest line in the title, and adding lines below it leaves the icon where it is. Settings → Icon lines up with also offers **Last line of the title**, which counts from the end of the words and puts a side icon after that line’s last word, and **Middle of the whole title**, which centres the icon on all the lines together and measures a side icon from the widest line."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:267
msgid "Measured again by itself"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:268
msgid "Placement is measured once your fonts load, when the window is resized and whenever the page changes, so a title that reflows puts the icon back without you doing anything."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:276
msgid "An icon inside a card"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:277
msgid "What happens when a widget card is narrower than the icon."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:283
msgid "Cards have no room to give"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:285
msgid "A post title may use the space your theme leaves beside it, but a card in a sidebar list or a slider does not own that space. Some themes cut off whatever leaves a card; the theme measured here does not, so an icon that cannot fit simply reaches past the edge. Either way the room beside the words is limited, which is why this setting exists."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:291
msgid "Off leaves the icon exactly as it is"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:296
msgid "With the switch off, nothing is resized: the icon keeps the size and offset you set, in every card. If the card is narrower than the icon and its gap, the icon reaches past the card edge, and your theme decides whether that part is shown."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:302
msgid "On fits the icon inside the card"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:307
msgid "With the switch on, an icon the card would cut off is drawn smaller, down to 8px, so it fits inside the card. The title is not touched: its words stay on the same line and are never indented, so the text keeps its full width. An icon is never hidden, and a card too narrow even for the smallest icon is left to clip. A post’s own title is not a card, so it keeps the page’s space whichever way the switch is set."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:315
#: blocks/shared/StageEditor.js:221
msgid "Size"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:316
msgid "How large the icon is drawn."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:321
msgid "Per stage"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:322
msgid "Sidebar → Size. A later stage can be bigger or smaller than the one before it."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:328
msgid "Empty means the asset’s size"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:333
msgid "Leave Size blank to use the size set on the asset itself, shown beside the field. Typing a number overrides it for that stage only."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:338
msgid "Units"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the default icon size, e.g. 20px.
#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:341
#, js-format
msgid "px, em, rem or %%. The default is %s. em sizes scale with the title, which keeps the icon in proportion as the heading grows."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:349
msgid "Following the title’s size"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:354
msgid "On a stage, choose Advanced (custom sizes) and the icon is sized from a table of title sizes and icon sizes, which appears only once you choose it: each row sets the icon size for titles from that title size up to the next row, so rows of 32 → 32 and 40 → 45 draw a 32px icon beside every title from 32px to 39px and a 45px one from 40px up. A title smaller than every row uses the first row’s icon, a larger one uses the last. The table starts from a copy of the site’s numbers under Settings → Title size → icon size, and editing one gives this stage its own table. A stage set to a fixed size keeps its own size instead."
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:359
msgid "Resizing keeps its place"
msgstr ""

#: blocks/admin/Guide.js:360
msgid "The icon stays centred on the title’s line and keeps its own space, so a size change never draws it over the words. Up to 20px it grows and shrinks about its middle; larger icons grow away from the title. It looks the same in the editor, in this sidebar’s preview, on your site and in widget titles such as the Posts Slider."
msgstr ""

